# Build context hygiene for `docker build` / `docker compose build`.
# Both images use the repo root as their context, so keep it lean and never
# ship host-installed node_modules (they would shadow the in-image pnpm install)
# or any local secrets / runtime state.

# Dependencies — always reinstalled inside the image from the frozen lockfile.
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
.pnpm

# Build outputs — regenerated in the build stage.
**/dist
**/build
**/out
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Git + agent worktrees (worktrees are huge and self-referential).
.git
.gitignore
.worktrees

# Self-hosted runtime state — must come from the named volume, not the context.
**/data
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-*
**/repos

# Secrets / local env — never bake into an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/session.secret

# Docker + CI assets that don't belong inside the image.
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.github

# Editor / OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Docs & planning material — not needed to build or run the apps.
docs
plans
*.md
